\]
So $O=\left(\dfrac{11}{4},2\right)$ and the radius is $\sqrt{\dfrac{25}{16}+4}=\dfrac{\sqrt{89}}{4}$. (Check: $OF^2=\left(\dfrac{47}{20}\right)^2+\left(\dfrac{1}{5}\right)^2=\dfrac{2225}{400}=\dfrac{89}{16}$, so $F$ is on the circle too.)

