The angle $72^\circ$ is not needed. Let the area of $ABC$ be $1$.

\textbf{Locating $F$.} Assign masses $A:1$, $C:1$ (so $E$, the midpoint of $AC$, has mass $2$) and $B:2$ (so that $2\cdot BD=1\cdot DC$, and $D$ has mass $3$). The balance point $F$ of the system lies on $BE$ and on $AD$, with
\[
\dfrac{BF}{FE}=\dfrac{2}{2}=1,\qquad\dfrac{AF}{FD}=\dfrac{3}{1}.
\]
\textbf{Areas.} $[ABD]=\dfrac{BD}{BC}[ABC]=\dfrac{1}{3}$ and $[BDF]=\dfrac{FD}{AD}[ABD]=\dfrac{1}{4}\cdot\dfrac{1}{3}=\dfrac{1}{12}$. Also $[BEC]=\dfrac{1}{2}$ because $E$ is the midpoint of $AC$, and the quadrilateral is
\[
[FDCE]=[BEC]-[BDF]=\dfrac{1}{2}-\dfrac{1}{12}=\dfrac{5}{12}.
\]

