\end{asy}

Hence $[BDF]:[FDCE]=\dfrac{1}{12}:\dfrac{5}{12}=\boxed{1:5}$.

Let $AD=BC=x$. In a right triangle each leg is the geometric mean of the hypotenuse and its projection on the hypotenuse (triangles $CBD$ and $ABC$ are similar, as are $ACD$ and $ABC$):
\[
BC^2=BD\cdot AB,\qquad AC^2=AD\cdot AB .
\]

