The fence has length $\boxed{18+12\pi}$ inches (about $55.7$ inches).

Place $A=(0,0)$ and $C=(10,0)$, and let $B=(p,q)$ with $q>0$. Then $p^2+q^2=529$ and $(p-10)^2+q^2=625$; subtracting gives $-20p+100=96$, so $p=\dfrac{1}{5}$ and
\[
q^2=529-\dfrac{1}{25}=\dfrac{13224}{25},\qquad q=\dfrac{2\sqrt{3306}}{5}
\]
(as $13224=4\cdot3306$). Now:
\begin{itemize}
\item $D=\dfrac{B+C}{2}=\left(\dfrac{51}{10},\dfrac {q}{2}\right)$;
\item $E=\left(\dfrac{1}{5},0\right)$, since $AC$ lies on the $x$-axis (and $0<\dfrac{1}{5}<10$, so $E$ is on side $AC$);
\item by the angle bisector theorem $\dfrac{AF}{FB}=\dfrac{CA}{CB}=\dfrac{10}{25}=\dfrac{2}{5}$, so $F=\dfrac{2}{7}B=\left(\dfrac{2}{35},\dfrac{2q}{7}\right)$.
\end{itemize}

